        "text": "Books"
      },
      {
        "type": "CustomEntry",
        "epId": 10484,
        "name": "Vera's Melancholy: Final Volume (Version I)",
        "desc": "It is said that the author of this work has rather questionable professional ethics — allegedly, the same story has been pitched to publishers as a \"new work\" again and again on various planets. This is perhaps the reason a kill order has been placed on the writer by a certain galactic empire.<br>Yu Huangyi cannot tell which volume was a piece of space debris salvaged by the mistress's sisters, and which was written by Hilda out of outrage at the original ending. After all, both are handwritten manuscripts...",
        "iconUrl": "https://act-webstatic.hoyoverse.com/event-static-hoyowiki-admin/2026/04/09/25b98e5e9035d6695a543b13e02c1025_3903866112938827945.png",
        "displayStyle": "card",
        "menuId": 9
      },
      {
        "type": "CustomEntry",
        "epId": 10485,
        "name": "Vera's Melancholy: Final Volume (Version II)",
        "desc": "The manuscript for the final volume of the \"Vera's Melancholy\" series. It was never published, however, because the author's portrayal of a certain princess from a galactic empire incurred enormous resentment from the princess who inspired the character. But somehow, the manuscript has found its way here.<br>Yu Huangyi cannot tell which volume was a piece of space debris salvaged by the mistress's sisters, and which was written by Hilda out of outrage at the original ending. After all, both are handwritten manuscripts...",
        "iconUrl": "https://act-webstatic.hoyoverse.com/event-static-hoyowiki-admin/2026/04/09/25b98e5e9035d6695a543b13e02c1025_3903866112938827945.png",
